course: dictionary
lesson: 13396
title: Hellenic: Greece and its past
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: «Hellenic» is an adjective. It tells you that something is to do with Greece and the Greek people. The Greeks called their own land Hellas, so Hellenic comes from that old name.
explain: Use the words around it as clues. «We studied Hellenic culture today: Greek poems, plays and statues.» Culture, poems, plays and statues tell you that Hellenic means about the arts and way of life of Greece.
explain: In history lessons, Hellenic often means ancient Greece, the time before Alexander the Great. Later Greek times are called Hellenistic, so check which word fits before you choose.
fact: «Hellenic» means to do with Greece and the Greek people, language and culture.
fact: In history, «Hellenic» often means classical Greek civilisation before Alexander the Great.
fact: Hellas is the name the Greeks gave to their own land.
fact: The modern country's official name is the Hellenic Republic.
fact: Later times are called «Hellenistic», so the two words are not the same.
exercise: «We studied Hellenic culture today: Greek poems, plays and statues.» What does Hellenic mean here? | To do with the sea only | A type of cake | To do with ancient Rome | *To do with ancient Greece
exercise: Which country does «the Hellenic Navy» belong to? | *Greece | Spain | Italy | Turkey
exercise: «Hellenic» comes from Hellas. What is Hellas? | A kind of Greek pottery | A famous Greek writer | *The Greeks' own name for their land | A cold island far to the north
test: In history, what does Hellenic usually point to? | Later Greek times after Alexander, called Hellenistic | Modern Italy | *Classical Greece, before Alexander the Great | The Roman Empire
test: What is the official name of modern Greece? | The Roman Republic | The Persian Republic | The Hellenistic Republic | *The Hellenic Republic
exam: In «a book about Hellenic culture», what does Hellenic mean? | To do with snow and ice | *To do with Greece and its people, language and culture | To do with cooking pasta | To do with trains and buses
